      "hints": [
        "Express $S_{10} = S_{15} - S_{10} \\implies 2S_{10} = S_{15}$.",
        "Substitute AP formulas: $10(2a + 9d) = 7.5(2a + 14d)$ and simplify to $d = \\frac{1}{3}a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the condition that the sum of the first 10 terms equals the sum of the next 5 terms (terms 11 to 15):\n$$S_{10} = S_{15} - S_{10} \\implies 2S_{10} = S_{15}$$",
        "Substitute the arithmetic series sum formula $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2a + (n - 1)d]$:\n$$2 \\times \\frac{10}{2}[2a + 9d] = \\frac{15}{2}[2a + 14d]$$\n$$10(2a + 9d) = 7.5(2a + 14d)$$\n$$20a + 90d = 15a + 105d$$",
        "Collect like terms:\n$$20a - 15a = 105d - 90d \\implies 5a = 15d \\implies d = \\frac{1}{3}a$$"
      ],
