        "Use $S_\\infty = 9S_4 \\implies \\frac{a}{1 - r} = 9\\frac{a(1 - r^4)}{1 - r} \\implies 1 = 9(1 - r^4)$.",
        "Find $r^4 = \\frac{8}{9}$, then calculate the 5th term $u_5 = ar^4 = 12\\left(\\frac{8}{9}\\right) = \\frac{32}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up the given relation $S_\\infty = 9S_4$ using the geometric series sum formulas:\n$$\\frac{a}{1 - r} = 9 \\times \\frac{a(1 - r^4)}{1 - r}$$",
        "Cancel the non-zero common factor $\\frac{a}{1 - r}$ from both sides:\n$$1 = 9(1 - r^4) \\implies 1 - r^4 = \\frac{1}{9} \\implies r^4 = 1 - \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{8}{9}$$",
        "Calculate the fifth term $u_5 = ar^4$ using $a = 12$:\n$$u_5 = 12 \\times \\frac{8}{9} = \\frac{96}{9} = \\frac{32}{3} = 10\\frac{2}{3} \\quad (\\approx 10.7)$$"
